{"operations":[{"content":"def is_valid(number: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if the provided number string is valid per the Luhn algorithm.\"\"\"\n    # Remove spaces\n    number = number.replace(' ', '')\n    if not number.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    total = 0\n    # Process digits from right to left\n    # The rightmost digit is the check digit and is not doubled\n    # Double every second digit from the right (indexing from 0)\n    digits = list(map(int, number))\n    length = len(digits)\n\n    for i in range(length - 1, -1, -1):\n        digit = digits[i]\n        # Determine if this digit should be doubled\n        # Double every second digit from the right, excluding the check digit\n        if (length - 1 - i) % 2 == 1:\n            digit *= 2\n            if digit > 9:\n                digit -= 9\n        total += digit\n\n    return total % 10 == 0\n","expected_sha256":"daa56df7794aa8b4da213da4d9fdee84518147a03a7f4ee745a11a06b101c3b1","kind":"modify","path":"src/luhn.py"}],"rationale":"Fixed the doubling logic in is_valid to correctly double every second digit from the right, excluding the check digit (rightmost digit), as per the Luhn algorithm specification. This ensures that the example 16-digit number '4539 1488 0343 6467' is valid and '4539 1488 0343 6468' is invalid, while preserving the public API and existing tests."}